{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>shall add days</b> — for a person's days are not fixed, but are according to nature, and nature will overcome and persist according to proper deeds; and the proof: \"that your days may be long.\" And what He said, \"I will fulfill the number of your days\" — these are according to what he can live by his nature, for they are in number." "<b>shall be shortened</b> — from the time he could live, for HaShem will weaken his strength or put them to death by means of mishap and accident, because they do not fear Him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:00.631958721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}